exp="The SVT family: <b>sinus tachycardia</b> (the <b>most common SVT</b>, so always ask why: fever, pain, anemia, hypovolemia, hyperthyroidism), atrial tachycardia (one irritable focus), flutter and AF, <b>AVNRT</b> (which the lecturer called the 2nd most common arrhythmia), junctional ectopic tachycardia (uncommon, mostly children), and AVRT (using an accessory pathway, as in WPW). \"SVT\" only tells you the rhythm starts above the ventricles. You still need the specific diagnosis.<br><br><b>Educational objective:</b> Sinus tachycardia is the most common SVT, so always look for its cause. \"SVT\" is a category, not a diagnosis.",
